.Dd August 20, 2026
.Dt CAIRN.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cairn.conf
.Nd configuration file for cairnd
.Sh DESCRIPTION
One
.Ql key = value
per line.
A
.Ql #
starts a comment and runs to the end of the line.
Blank lines are ignored.
An unknown key is an error, not a warning: a typo in a limit must not silently
leave it at its default.
.Pp
Sizes accept a
.Ql K ,
.Ql M
or
.Ql G
suffix and are otherwise decimal bytes.
Durations accept
.Ql ms ,
.Ql s
or
.Ql m ;
a bare number is seconds.
Booleans are
.Ql on
or
.Ql off .
.Sh LISTENING
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic listen No = Ar unix:PATH | tcp:ADDR
Default
.Ql unix:/run/cairn/cairn.sock .
A TCP address must be loopback; anything else is refused at startup.
TLS is the reverse proxy's job.
.It Ic socket_mode No = Ar OCTAL
Mode of the unix socket, applied after binding.
Default
.Ql 0660 .
.El
.Sh ARCHIVES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic archive_dir No = Ar PATH
Directory of
.Pa *.zim
files, not descended into.
Default
.Pa /var/lib/cairn/archives .
This is the only path Landlock leaves readable.
.It Ic max_cluster_bytes No = Ar SIZE
Ceiling on one decompressed cluster.
Default
.Ql 32M .
A crafted cluster cannot exhaust memory: the decoder is stopped at the bound
rather than checked after the fact.
.It Ic cluster_cache_bytes No = Ar SIZE
Global budget for decoded cluster bodies, shared by every archive.
Default
.Ql 64M .
This is the ceiling on the amplification a client gets by asking repeatedly for
a tiny entry inside a large compressed cluster.
Uncompressed clusters are served straight from the mapping and never enter it.
.It Ic max_metadata_bytes No = Ar SIZE
Ceiling on one
.Ql M
namespace value.
Default
.Ql 8K .
.It Ic max_metadata_entries No = Ar N
Ceiling on how many metadata entries are reported.
Default
.Ql 64 .
.El
.Sh CONFINEMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic sandbox No = Ar require | best-effort | off
Default
.Ql best-effort :
apply what the kernel offers and report the rest.
.Ql require
refuses to start unless every enabled layer applied.
.Ql off
applies nothing and logs a warning.
.It Ic sandbox_landlock No = Ar on | off
Default
.Ql on .
Turning it off with
.Ql sandbox require
means the requirement covers the remaining layers only.
.It Ic sandbox_seccomp No = Ar on | off
Default
.Ql on .
.It Ic sandbox_action No = Ar kill | errno | log
What the kernel does with a syscall outside the allowlist.
Default
.Ql kill .
.Ql errno
fails the call with
.Er EPERM
and is how you find a missing entry on an unfamiliar kernel;
.Ql log
allows it.
Neither belongs in production.
.El
.Sh AUTHENTICATION
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic auth_token No = Ar TOKEN
A single shared bearer token.
Unset by default, which means no authentication.
There are no accounts, sessions or roles.
.It Ic auth_token_file No = Ar PATH
Read the token from a file instead, trimming whitespace.
Read once, at startup, before confinement.
Prefer this: it keeps the token out of a world-readable config.
.El
.Sh CONNECTION LIMITS
None of these is unbounded.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic max_connections No = Ar N
Worker threads, and therefore the ceiling on concurrent connections.
Default
.Ql 64 .
Further connections wait in the kernel's accept queue.
Threads are created before confinement and never after.
.It Ic read_timeout No = Ar DURATION
Time allowed to send a request.
Default
.Ql 15s .
A half-written request is answered
.Ql 408
and dropped.
.It Ic write_timeout No = Ar DURATION
Time allowed to accept a response.
Default
.Ql 30s .
.It Ic keepalive_requests No = Ar N
Requests per connection before it is closed.
Default
.Ql 100 .
.It Ic keepalive_timeout No = Ar DURATION
Idle time allowed between requests on a connection.
Default
.Ql 15s .
.It Ic request_rate No = Ar N
Requests per second per connection, as a token bucket.
Default
.Ql 50 .
Zero disables the ceiling.
.It Ic request_burst No = Ar N
Bucket depth.
Default
.Ql 100 .
.El
.Sh REQUEST LIMITS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic max_request_line No = Ar SIZE
Default
.Ql 8K .
Longer is
.Ql 414 .
.It Ic max_header_bytes No = Ar SIZE
Default
.Ql 16K .
Longer is
.Ql 431 .
.It Ic max_headers No = Ar N
Default
.Ql 64 .
.It Ic max_path_bytes No = Ar SIZE
Ceiling on a decoded entry path.
Default
.Ql 1K .
.It Ic suggest_max_query No = Ar SIZE
Ceiling on
.Ql q .
Default
.Ql 128 .
.It Ic suggest_max_results No = Ar N
Ceiling on suggestions returned.
Default
.Ql 32 .
.El
.Sh RESPONSES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic content_security_policy No = Ar VALUE
Sent with entry content.
Default
.Ql default-src 'none'; sandbox .
A control byte in the value is a startup error.
This does not make archived HTML safe to render in your own origin; see
.Xr cairn-api 7 .
.El
.Sh LOGGING
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic log_level No = Ar error | warn | info | debug
Default
.Ql info .
.It Ic access_log No = Ar on | off
Default
.Ql off .
When on, each request logs method, status, body size and duration.
The request target is never logged: it is client input.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
An offline appliance serving one directory to local programs:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
listen = unix:/run/cairn/cairn.sock
socket_mode = 0660
archive_dir = /srv/zim
sandbox = require
max_connections = 32
cluster_cache_bytes = 128M
.Ed
.Pp
Behind a reverse proxy on loopback, with a token:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
listen = tcp:127.0.0.1:8320
auth_token_file = /etc/cairn/token
request_rate = 20
request_burst = 40
access_log = on
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cairn 1 ,
.Xr cairn-api 7 ,
.Xr cairnd 8
